1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:11,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:12,909 --> 00:00:16,538
Amazing! It's like
we stepped inside the painting.

3
00:00:18,915 --> 00:00:24,504
Strong, vivid colors
that envelop the entire body.

4
00:00:25,088 --> 00:00:29,217
-In short, basically, well…
-It's the best, right?

5
00:00:29,759 --> 00:00:30,885
Yes.

6
00:00:32,053 --> 00:00:33,555
It's the best.

7
00:00:34,139 --> 00:00:36,516
That reminds me.
Why did you invite me here?

8
00:00:37,183 --> 00:00:40,895
You told me before
that you were interested in digital art.

9
00:00:41,729 --> 00:00:43,648
That's sweet.

10
00:00:45,441 --> 00:00:47,986
But Mori, don't you ever go
on dates with a boyfriend?

11
00:00:48,069 --> 00:00:49,279
A boyfriend?

12
00:00:51,281 --> 00:00:52,282
A date?

13
00:00:52,991 --> 00:00:55,368
Are you just not interested in romance?

14
00:00:55,451 --> 00:00:56,911
Romance.

15
00:00:56,995 --> 00:01:00,540
Love and affection?

16
00:01:01,791 --> 00:01:02,709
I am interested in it.

17
00:01:03,334 --> 00:01:04,502
You are, huh?

18
00:01:05,253 --> 00:01:06,921
So, what's your type, then?

19
00:01:07,005 --> 00:01:10,967
However, I have yet to define
what romance is.

20
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:14,137
Who cares about the definition?

21
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:15,138
Love.

22
00:01:17,056 --> 00:01:18,808
What is it, I wonder.

23
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:26,190
‎There is major rainfall tonight

24
00:01:26,274 --> 00:01:28,735
‎in Tokyo Prefecture
‎and Kanagawa Prefecture.

25
00:01:28,818 --> 00:01:31,654
‎It is also highly likely
‎there has already been flooding…

26
00:01:31,738 --> 00:01:34,073
Oh man! Oh man!

27
00:01:34,782 --> 00:01:36,451
Hey, you're soaked!

28
00:01:36,534 --> 00:01:38,411
It's a total downpour outside!

29
00:01:38,494 --> 00:01:40,663
The link bridge has a lot of water
flowing through it.

30
00:01:40,747 --> 00:01:42,874
The drainage can't keep up at all.

31
00:01:42,957 --> 00:01:44,709
Dang, it's flooding?

32
00:01:44,792 --> 00:01:46,377
This area was built in a rush after all.

33
00:01:46,461 --> 00:01:47,545
Ah, thank you.

34
00:01:47,629 --> 00:01:51,382
Let's just go home. All flights
must be canceled now, right?

35
00:01:53,635 --> 00:01:54,761
Yes?

36
00:01:56,804 --> 00:01:57,722
Yes.

37
00:01:59,724 --> 00:02:03,436
Flight UNT815 from the Unitia Federation
will be landing shortly.

38
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:05,980
-What?
-Seriously? In this rain?

39
00:02:06,064 --> 00:02:08,942
-The captain really did their best.
-This is the last flight of the day.

40
00:02:09,025 --> 00:02:10,944
Yes, let's wrap it up smoothly
and go home!

41
00:02:13,613 --> 00:02:14,822
Is love…

42
00:02:18,117 --> 00:02:20,370
a torrential downpour?

43
00:02:20,453 --> 00:02:21,579
You're still thinking about that?

44
00:02:22,872 --> 00:02:24,666
Hurry, let's go.

45
00:02:24,749 --> 00:02:25,750
Yes.

46
00:02:34,968 --> 00:02:36,219
Just this way.

47
00:02:37,387 --> 00:02:38,638
-Two booths, open.
-Please don't rush.

48
00:02:38,721 --> 00:02:39,681
So next in line, please.

49
00:02:39,764 --> 00:02:42,100
-Please be careful.
-Just this way.

50
00:02:42,183 --> 00:02:44,644
-It's okay. Don't worry.
-Next in line, please.

51
00:02:44,727 --> 00:02:47,313
Please watch your step.

52
00:02:48,314 --> 00:02:49,273
This way, please.

53
00:02:49,357 --> 00:02:51,150
-Please watch your step.
-Let's go.

54
00:02:55,196 --> 00:02:56,322
Japanese is fine.

55
00:02:56,406 --> 00:02:58,491
He's third-generation Japanese.

56
00:02:58,574 --> 00:03:01,911
Speaks fluent Japanese too, right?

57
00:03:01,995 --> 00:03:03,997
We're engaged.

58
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,832
We're traveling before our wedding.

59
00:03:05,915 --> 00:03:08,251
I see. Well then, your passports, please.

60
00:03:08,334 --> 00:03:09,252
-Here.
-Thank you.

61
00:03:09,836 --> 00:03:11,546
-I'll just hold it to the glass.
-Be gentle.

62
00:03:11,629 --> 00:03:12,505
-We'll need it later.
-Yes.

63
00:03:12,588 --> 00:03:14,632
-Wonderful.
-Wonderful.

64
00:03:14,716 --> 00:03:17,468
Leon Araki and Aoi Onodera.

65
00:03:17,552 --> 00:03:20,430
Leon, you are visiting for tourism.

66
00:03:20,513 --> 00:03:21,681
How long is your stay?

67
00:03:23,474 --> 00:03:25,727
Wherever the wind blows,
wherever the stones call.

68
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:26,644
IMMIGRATION OFFICER, MINISTRY OF JUSTICE
AKIHIKO SEIKE

69
00:03:26,728 --> 00:03:29,439
-Stones?
-He is a gem appraiser.

70
00:03:29,522 --> 00:03:30,982
He travels all around the world.

71
00:03:32,066 --> 00:03:35,278
I run a jewelry company myself,

72
00:03:35,361 --> 00:03:37,780
so we really hit it off.

73
00:03:37,864 --> 00:03:39,657
-We did.
-We did!

74
00:03:39,741 --> 00:03:42,994
And then, I found a gem named Aoi.

75
00:03:44,078 --> 00:03:46,331
Stop it, Leon.

76
00:03:47,623 --> 00:03:49,834
Look, this is the engagement ring
he gave me.

77
00:03:49,917 --> 00:03:51,836
How wonderful.

78
00:03:51,919 --> 00:03:53,254
So, how long is your stay?

79
00:03:54,088 --> 00:03:56,632
-About two weeks, right?
-Ah, yes.

80
00:03:56,716 --> 00:03:57,967
I guess so.

81
00:03:58,051 --> 00:04:00,678
Excuse me. I'll inspect your luggage now.

82
00:04:00,762 --> 00:04:01,679
Yes.

83
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,686
Is that also a form of love?

84
00:04:10,063 --> 00:04:11,147
Pardon?

85
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:12,398
KEIICHIRO HAYAMI - IMMIGRATION OFFICIAL

86
00:04:17,236 --> 00:04:21,115
-What is this?
-That is a fountain pen.

87
00:04:21,199 --> 00:04:23,076
Adorned with gold and natural gems,

88
00:04:23,159 --> 00:04:26,579
passed down from the former
royal family of the Unitia Federation.

89
00:04:29,082 --> 00:04:30,124
Here you go.

90
00:04:31,542 --> 00:04:35,046
Excuse me, but approximately
how much is it worth?

91
00:04:37,006 --> 00:04:39,801
High-value items
may be subject to taxation.

92
00:04:40,968 --> 00:04:44,639
Oh, well, you cannot put a price tag
on something like this.

93
00:04:45,598 --> 00:04:47,266
That's not what I mean.

94
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:50,269
-What?
-The interior work is falling behind.

95
00:04:50,853 --> 00:04:52,688
We have less than a year
until the opening, you know?

96
00:04:53,481 --> 00:04:56,484
Miss, please refrain from having
phone calls in the inspection area.

97
00:04:57,276 --> 00:04:59,612
Send me the progress report later.

98
00:05:06,452 --> 00:05:08,746
I've seen her before.

99
00:05:08,830 --> 00:05:10,873
That's Toko Tsuzuki, the entrepreneur.

100
00:05:11,541 --> 00:05:15,211
She's super talented.
She made her mark revitalizing hotels.

101
00:05:29,642 --> 00:05:31,978
You are Ms. Toko Tsuzuki

102
00:05:39,152 --> 00:05:42,738
I plan to get my medical license
in Japan, so…

103
00:05:42,822 --> 00:05:45,783
He is a resident doctor
in the Unitia Federation.

104
00:05:46,367 --> 00:05:48,369
Do you have documents
from your place of study?

105
00:05:48,452 --> 00:05:49,537
Ah, yes.

106
00:05:53,583 --> 00:05:54,500
Thank you.

107
00:05:54,584 --> 00:05:55,751
Go ahead.

108
00:05:55,835 --> 00:05:57,837
-I will inspect your luggage.
-Okay.

109
00:05:58,546 --> 00:05:59,672
All right.

110
00:05:59,755 --> 00:06:01,132
-Thank you.
-Thanks.

111
00:06:02,091 --> 00:06:04,844
-Now, please head over there.
-Okay.

112
00:06:08,347 --> 00:06:10,141
Ah, sorry, one at a time.

113
00:06:14,896 --> 00:06:15,897
One more time.

114
00:06:17,273 --> 00:06:18,107
Um…

115
00:06:19,150 --> 00:06:21,027
-What are these?
-Vitamins.

116
00:06:21,110 --> 00:06:24,614
He says they're good
for health and beauty.

117
00:06:24,697 --> 00:06:26,908
Those are only supplements.

118
00:06:26,991 --> 00:06:30,244
Do you have the original container
that shows the ingredients?

119
00:06:32,121 --> 00:06:33,039
I threw it away.

120
00:06:33,706 --> 00:06:36,584
We will need to confirm if these
are permitted entry into the country.

121
00:06:38,169 --> 00:06:39,086
Excuse me.

122
00:06:39,170 --> 00:06:41,964
I also have a few things
I'd like to confirm about Mr. Luca.

123
00:06:42,048 --> 00:06:43,299
Let's step into the secondary room.

124
00:06:44,091 --> 00:06:45,051
The secondary room?

125
00:06:45,134 --> 00:06:47,261
Sorry for the trouble.
Take them to the secondary room.

126
00:06:47,345 --> 00:06:48,512
Okay.

127
00:06:48,596 --> 00:06:50,264
I'll carry your bags.

128
00:06:52,516 --> 00:06:53,768
Excuse me.

129
00:06:53,851 --> 00:06:56,229
I need to get back to the office soon.

130
00:07:03,736 --> 00:07:05,404
Um, please hurry.

131
00:07:05,488 --> 00:07:07,198
Yes, yes, this way.

132
00:07:07,782 --> 00:07:09,283
Hurry! You too, Luca!

133
00:07:16,582 --> 00:07:17,917
What's that?

134
00:07:22,838 --> 00:07:24,340
You found it.

135
00:07:30,096 --> 00:07:31,389
Toko.

136
00:07:32,014 --> 00:07:34,976
I was going to give this
to you in private, but…

137
00:07:38,896 --> 00:07:40,648
Could that be…

138
00:07:40,731 --> 00:07:42,858
-No way, a proposal?
-Right here?

139
00:07:42,942 --> 00:07:45,194
Oh my.

140
00:07:52,118 --> 00:07:55,037
Toko, my love,

141
00:07:55,788 --> 00:07:57,498
you've always been there for me.

142
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,334
Now I want to be there for you.

143
00:08:01,335 --> 00:08:03,170
Will you marry me?

144
00:08:05,506 --> 00:08:07,883
-Whoa!
-What happened?

145
00:08:07,967 --> 00:08:10,052
Please stay calm!
Power will be restored shortly!

146
00:08:10,136 --> 00:08:12,305
Please do not move from where you are!

147
00:08:12,388 --> 00:08:13,639
POWER OUTAGE

148
00:08:15,266 --> 00:08:16,183
EMERGENCY POWER

149
00:08:16,267 --> 00:08:17,351
Toko?

150
00:08:19,562 --> 00:08:21,188
Let go of me!

151
00:08:21,272 --> 00:08:23,190
-What are you doing?
-Stay back!

152
00:08:23,274 --> 00:08:24,358
Don't get any closer.

153
00:08:24,442 --> 00:08:26,736
Fine! Please calm down.

154
00:08:26,819 --> 00:08:28,904
-Come on!
-Everyone, please back away!

155
00:08:28,988 --> 00:08:30,239
-Get back!
-Everyone, get back!

156
00:08:30,323 --> 00:08:31,782
-Get back!
-Let's calm down.

157
00:08:31,866 --> 00:08:33,868
-Get back!
-Gate 24 Inspection Booth,

158
00:08:33,951 --> 00:08:35,578
a man has restrained a female passenger.

159
00:08:36,746 --> 00:08:38,748
Come on. Get back!

160
00:08:42,043 --> 00:08:43,669
Wait…

161
00:08:43,753 --> 00:08:45,171
-Wait…
-Toko!

162
00:08:45,254 --> 00:08:47,089
Hey, hey, hey! Get back.

163
00:08:47,173 --> 00:08:48,215
That's my fountain pen! Excuse me…

164
00:08:48,299 --> 00:08:49,675
-Give that back!
-Stop!

165
00:08:49,759 --> 00:08:51,260
-Get back!
-Stop!

166
00:08:52,511 --> 00:08:53,763
You little…

167
00:08:57,058 --> 00:08:58,184
Hayami!

168
00:09:01,604 --> 00:09:02,480
No one come in!

169
00:09:03,397 --> 00:09:04,815
Next time, I'll really stab someone!

170
00:09:07,526 --> 00:09:10,237
-Are you okay?
-Thank you.

171
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:12,907
You're a doctor, right?

172
00:09:12,990 --> 00:09:14,950
-Could you examine him?
-Sure.

173
00:09:15,034 --> 00:09:15,951
Don't move!

174
00:09:17,745 --> 00:09:18,954
I don't trust you.

175
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:21,040
Gunji.

176
00:09:21,707 --> 00:09:22,958
How did you find me here?

177
00:09:25,086 --> 00:09:26,337
D-Do you know each other?

178
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:31,342
He's a former coworker.

179
00:09:32,051 --> 00:09:33,761
Ex-boyfriend.

180
00:09:35,554 --> 00:09:36,514
Right?

181
00:09:38,474 --> 00:09:40,518
I came here to protect you.

182
00:09:41,435 --> 00:09:42,353
Because

183
00:09:43,354 --> 00:09:44,605
I still love you.

184
00:09:49,402 --> 00:09:51,112
Is this also…

185
00:09:52,905 --> 00:09:54,156
love?

186
00:10:03,124 --> 00:10:05,084
The meeting just ended.

187
00:10:05,167 --> 00:10:07,294
The airport director is here too.

188
00:10:07,378 --> 00:10:09,171
Please tell me the situation.

189
00:10:09,255 --> 00:10:12,216
The man is Ryosuke Gunji.
Using a fountain pen, he has taken

190
00:10:12,299 --> 00:10:14,802
two passengers and two staff hostage
and barricaded himself in.

191
00:10:14,885 --> 00:10:16,137
Passengers are being held hostage.

192
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:17,638
What about the other passengers?

193
00:10:17,722 --> 00:10:20,307
We evacuated them to the waiting area.

194
00:10:20,391 --> 00:10:22,727
-However…
-The link bridge is flooded,

195
00:10:22,810 --> 00:10:24,395
so reinforcements can't make it through.

196
00:10:24,478 --> 00:10:26,856
My valuable fountain pen is in there!

197
00:10:26,939 --> 00:10:28,315
Get it back quickly!

198
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:30,192
-Please calm down.
-Leon!

199
00:10:34,488 --> 00:10:37,950
A tactical unit is heading your way now.

200
00:10:38,033 --> 00:10:40,077
However, due to the heavy rain,

201
00:10:40,161 --> 00:10:42,246
it will take them about an hour to arrive.

202
00:10:42,329 --> 00:10:43,622
That long?

203
00:10:44,123 --> 00:10:45,374
What about Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa?

204
00:10:45,458 --> 00:10:47,835
He's at the main Immigration Bureau
and can't reach you.

205
00:10:47,918 --> 00:10:49,086
Neither can we.

206
00:10:49,170 --> 00:10:52,798
Until reinforcements arrive,
the remaining personnel must hold out.

207
00:10:52,882 --> 00:10:54,133
Understood.

208
00:10:54,884 --> 00:10:56,093
One hour.

209
00:10:57,219 --> 00:10:59,513
So this place will be
an isolated island until then?

210
00:10:59,597 --> 00:11:01,849
‎GATE24-SECONDARY ROOM

211
00:11:08,439 --> 00:11:10,357
Don't answer that! Decline it!

212
00:11:10,441 --> 00:11:12,026
Okay, okay.

213
00:11:12,109 --> 00:11:13,861
Stop yelling at every little thing.

214
00:11:14,403 --> 00:11:16,739
-Are you all right, Luca?
-Hey, move away!

215
00:11:16,822 --> 00:11:19,658
-Stop cuddling up.
-What's the problem?

216
00:11:20,159 --> 00:11:22,286
Hey, hey! Don't move.

217
00:11:22,369 --> 00:11:24,413
May I clean up the luggage?

218
00:11:25,789 --> 00:11:28,501
We should take care of the belongings.

219
00:11:28,584 --> 00:11:29,502
Hey…

220
00:11:29,585 --> 00:11:31,086
-Mori…
-Hayami.

221
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:34,673
It will take one hour
for the tactical unit to arrive.

222
00:11:34,757 --> 00:11:37,635
Please hold out until then.

223
00:11:54,818 --> 00:11:56,028
Hey, you!

224
00:11:56,946 --> 00:11:59,532
Gunji. You're Gunji, aren't you?

225
00:12:00,533 --> 00:12:02,451
Would you please talk to us?

226
00:12:03,661 --> 00:12:05,746
We are not your enemies.

227
00:12:05,829 --> 00:12:09,124
Our top priority is for everyone
to get out of here safely.

228
00:12:10,251 --> 00:12:12,836
I hear you're a former coworker
of Tsuzuki.

229
00:12:15,756 --> 00:12:16,840
Five years ago,

230
00:12:17,758 --> 00:12:20,177
we started a company together.

231
00:12:20,261 --> 00:12:23,180
But as soon as it got on track,
she kicked me out,

232
00:12:23,264 --> 00:12:24,765
claiming "differences in direction".

233
00:12:26,475 --> 00:12:29,687
-So you're doing this out of revenge?
-No!

234
00:12:30,354 --> 00:12:33,274
Someone from the old company
reached out to me.

235
00:12:33,357 --> 00:12:37,027
They said the CEO was recently obsessing
over a young foreigner.

236
00:12:37,903 --> 00:12:40,531
-You mean me?
-That's right.

237
00:12:40,614 --> 00:12:41,991
When did you start seeing this guy?

238
00:12:42,074 --> 00:12:46,120
A year ago, when she came
to Unitia on business.

239
00:12:47,079 --> 00:12:49,123
I suddenly felt unwell,

240
00:12:49,206 --> 00:12:51,709
and Luca, who happened to be
passing by, took care of me.

241
00:12:53,043 --> 00:12:55,004
A fateful meeting, you could call it.

242
00:12:56,130 --> 00:12:57,464
What fate?

243
00:12:58,882 --> 00:13:01,969
A young, handsome doctor
who just happened to be passing by?

244
00:13:02,052 --> 00:13:03,178
Who's madly in love with you?

245
00:13:03,262 --> 00:13:07,182
-How could anything be that convenient?
-It actually happened.

246
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:09,059
What?

247
00:13:10,019 --> 00:13:12,396
-Are you jealous?
-No, I am not.

248
00:13:13,105 --> 00:13:14,023
Let me tell you clearly.

249
00:13:14,106 --> 00:13:16,900
This guy is a marriage fraudster!

250
00:13:17,818 --> 00:13:19,486
A marriage fraudster?

251
00:13:19,570 --> 00:13:21,280
That's the only explanation.

252
00:13:21,363 --> 00:13:22,865
What he's after is money.

253
00:13:22,948 --> 00:13:25,701
That and status to live in Japan.

254
00:13:25,784 --> 00:13:27,119
What are you talking about?

255
00:13:27,703 --> 00:13:29,371
Things like that happen, right?

256
00:13:29,913 --> 00:13:33,125
Well, yes. There are cases
where foreign nationals

257
00:13:33,208 --> 00:13:36,170
attempt to illegally obtain residency
through fake marriages.

258
00:13:36,253 --> 00:13:38,380
-See?
-However,

259
00:13:38,464 --> 00:13:41,592
marriage does not automatically
guarantee permission to live in Japan.

260
00:13:41,675 --> 00:13:43,636
The actual reality of the marriage
and the couple's lives

261
00:13:43,719 --> 00:13:45,346
are strictly examined.

262
00:13:46,347 --> 00:13:47,264
Then

263
00:13:47,931 --> 00:13:50,726
perform that examination
right now, right here!

264
00:13:51,810 --> 00:13:52,645
Pardon?

265
00:13:52,728 --> 00:13:55,439
Expose the fact that this guy
is deceiving Toko.

266
00:13:55,522 --> 00:13:56,565
Until that's made clear,

267
00:13:57,191 --> 00:13:59,193
no one leaves this room!

268
00:14:00,069 --> 00:14:01,445
Examining…

269
00:14:02,821 --> 00:14:04,406
love?

270
00:14:04,990 --> 00:14:07,493
Luca is a scammer?

271
00:14:08,077 --> 00:14:10,913
And we have to examine it here?

272
00:14:13,874 --> 00:14:15,793
-The police, the police!
-Is it the tactical unit?

273
00:14:16,543 --> 00:14:17,836
They're here already?

274
00:14:26,553 --> 00:14:29,264
There, there, there!

275
00:14:30,766 --> 00:14:34,228
Ah, finally made it.

276
00:14:34,311 --> 00:14:35,604
-Iuchi?
-What? Yes.

277
00:14:35,688 --> 00:14:37,731
Huh? Where's the tactical unit?

278
00:14:37,815 --> 00:14:40,442
Not here yet. Only the two of us
were able to move ahead.

279
00:14:40,526 --> 00:14:43,529
Sorry, but we aren't here as your backup.

280
00:14:44,363 --> 00:14:46,657
-What?
-We were in the airport

281
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:48,826
investigating a separate matter.

282
00:14:49,618 --> 00:14:50,577
We got a tip-off.

283
00:14:50,661 --> 00:14:53,998
There's a possibility a marriage fraudster
is on this final flight.

284
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,960
Mori, what are you doing?

285
00:14:58,043 --> 00:14:59,628
Inspecting.

286
00:15:01,964 --> 00:15:05,217
Um, immigration is not a marriage agency,

287
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:06,927
nor can we evaluate human affection.

288
00:15:07,011 --> 00:15:10,431
Just investigate him! He's a scammer!

289
00:15:12,725 --> 00:15:14,309
Fine!

290
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:17,980
-If he insists, why not investigate?
-Um, like I said…

291
00:15:18,063 --> 00:15:20,441
You saw it earlier, didn't you?
Luca's proposal.

292
00:15:21,066 --> 00:15:22,651
That right there is proof of love.

293
00:15:24,903 --> 00:15:26,363
Proof of love.

294
00:15:40,169 --> 00:15:42,838
Toko, let me tell you this again.

295
00:15:45,049 --> 00:15:47,718
-Will you--
-Don't do it now!

296
00:15:47,801 --> 00:15:49,094
Um…

297
00:15:49,678 --> 00:15:50,846
Excuse me.

298
00:15:53,682 --> 00:15:55,642
That blue stone…

299
00:15:56,477 --> 00:15:57,519
It's a sapphire.

300
00:15:58,187 --> 00:15:59,646
I thought it'd look good on her.

301
00:16:00,731 --> 00:16:02,691
May I take a look at it?

302
00:16:06,737 --> 00:16:07,988
What are you doing?

303
00:16:13,786 --> 00:16:15,537
What are you doing?

304
00:16:16,663 --> 00:16:20,209
I can see a few tiny air bubbles
inside the stone.

305
00:16:20,292 --> 00:16:21,293
Air bubbles?

306
00:16:21,376 --> 00:16:24,254
Natural sapphires contain inclusions.

307
00:16:24,338 --> 00:16:27,049
However, having multiple
air bubbles like this

308
00:16:27,132 --> 00:16:29,343
is a characteristic
commonly seen in glass.

309
00:16:29,426 --> 00:16:31,303
Then that stone is…

310
00:16:31,386 --> 00:16:32,888
I cannot say for certain,

311
00:16:32,971 --> 00:16:36,767
but it may be a piece of glass,
made to imitate a sapphire.

312
00:16:38,227 --> 00:16:39,561
A fake?

313
00:16:41,271 --> 00:16:42,689
Is it this guy?

314
00:16:43,315 --> 00:16:44,483
See?

315
00:16:44,566 --> 00:16:47,069
He tried to trick you with a cheap ring!

316
00:16:47,152 --> 00:16:49,530
It hasn't been proven fake yet.

317
00:16:50,114 --> 00:16:52,908
Besides, the price doesn't matter.

318
00:16:53,534 --> 00:16:55,702
As long as his feelings
are genuine, that's enough.

319
00:16:56,745 --> 00:16:58,580
Um…

320
00:16:58,664 --> 00:17:03,043
Actually, there is
one more thing that concerns me.

321
00:17:03,627 --> 00:17:05,254
-One more thing?
-Yes.

322
00:17:05,337 --> 00:17:08,257
Earlier, the woman at the adjacent booth

323
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:10,843
was wearing a similar ring.

324
00:17:12,803 --> 00:17:15,556
-The woman next to us too?
-Yes.

325
00:17:16,181 --> 00:17:17,558
Were you aware of this?

326
00:17:19,309 --> 00:17:22,229
I don't know. Maybe it's a coincidence.

327
00:17:22,813 --> 00:17:24,565
That couple too?

328
00:17:25,274 --> 00:17:28,318
True, it is a similar ring.

329
00:17:28,402 --> 00:17:30,571
Now that you mention it, I saw something.

330
00:17:31,363 --> 00:17:32,906
During the proposal earlier.

331
00:17:39,288 --> 00:17:40,372
Luca and Leon?

332
00:17:41,498 --> 00:17:43,584
Those two might know each other.

333
00:17:44,877 --> 00:17:45,919
Iuchi.

334
00:17:47,629 --> 00:17:48,505
Could you folks

335
00:17:49,923 --> 00:17:51,508
help us out a bit?

336
00:17:56,555 --> 00:17:57,598
Leon.

337
00:17:57,681 --> 00:17:58,849
A conversation?

338
00:17:58,932 --> 00:18:01,602
Since the inspection
was interrupted earlier,

339
00:18:01,685 --> 00:18:03,937
-we'd like to continue.
-Is there still something else?

340
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:07,065
You mentioned you're engaged.

341
00:18:07,149 --> 00:18:10,360
When and how did you meet?

342
00:18:10,444 --> 00:18:11,695
It was fate.

343
00:18:11,778 --> 00:18:14,531
Just like how stones draw people in,
we were drawn to each other--

344
00:18:14,615 --> 00:18:16,033
A dating app.

345
00:18:16,116 --> 00:18:17,117
What?

346
00:18:18,243 --> 00:18:20,287
There's an app for celebrities.

347
00:18:20,370 --> 00:18:23,624
We messaged for about a week
and instantly hit it off.

348
00:18:23,707 --> 00:18:24,541
Right?

349
00:18:26,501 --> 00:18:29,087
-A dating app?
-That's right.

350
00:18:29,171 --> 00:18:32,007
When did you actually meet in person?

351
00:18:32,841 --> 00:18:35,260
-It's as if in a past life we knew--
-Three days ago.

352
00:18:35,844 --> 00:18:37,512
-What?
-What?

353
00:18:37,596 --> 00:18:40,182
I went all the way to Unitia,

354
00:18:40,265 --> 00:18:42,309
and that was our first meeting.

355
00:18:43,185 --> 00:18:47,147
The moment we met, we both knew
we were the one for each other.

356
00:18:48,732 --> 00:18:49,983
Time doesn't matter in love.

357
00:18:52,611 --> 00:18:55,572
They met through an app
and got engaged right away.

358
00:18:55,656 --> 00:18:57,866
There is being efficient,
and then there is this.

359
00:18:58,617 --> 00:19:02,579
Both of them got engaged
to Japanese corporate executives

360
00:19:02,663 --> 00:19:05,207
and gave them similar rings.

361
00:19:07,584 --> 00:19:08,752
These two…

362
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,005
might be in cahoots.

363
00:19:17,135 --> 00:19:18,428
METROPOLITAN POLICE DEPARTMENT

364
00:19:18,512 --> 00:19:21,348
Is the tactical unit still not there?

365
00:19:21,431 --> 00:19:22,724
Pacing around

366
00:19:23,517 --> 00:19:25,227
won't make them arrive any faster.

367
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:26,979
How can you remain so calm?

368
00:19:27,062 --> 00:19:28,522
It's a hostage situation!
A hostage situation!

369
00:19:28,605 --> 00:19:30,857
And it's terrible weather outside.

370
00:19:30,941 --> 00:19:33,527
Everything is completely unexpected.

371
00:19:33,610 --> 00:19:37,489
Crises always exceed expectations.

372
00:19:38,407 --> 00:19:40,450
Only our ground staff can deal with it.

373
00:19:41,243 --> 00:19:43,078
All we can do is trust them.

374
00:19:55,549 --> 00:19:57,259
Hayami, Mori.

375
00:19:57,342 --> 00:19:58,552
This is Iuchi from Tokyo Police.

376
00:20:00,220 --> 00:20:03,473
The guy named Luca there
and that guy Leon over here

377
00:20:03,557 --> 00:20:06,601
might belong to the same
marriage fraud ring.

378
00:20:08,270 --> 00:20:09,980
We checked Leon Araki,

379
00:20:10,063 --> 00:20:13,233
but found no record
of his activity as a gem appraiser.

380
00:20:14,318 --> 00:20:16,403
I'm just providing you with info.

381
00:20:16,486 --> 00:20:18,780
The tactical unit arrives in 20 minutes.

382
00:20:19,448 --> 00:20:21,992
Do not provoke the suspect
under any circumstances.

383
00:20:26,538 --> 00:20:28,790
Hey. What are you doing?

384
00:20:36,173 --> 00:20:37,341
Take it off.

385
00:20:37,424 --> 00:20:38,467
You too, off!

386
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:52,439
That was close.

387
00:20:53,231 --> 00:20:54,983
Audio is still being picked up.

388
00:20:55,067 --> 00:20:57,652
But they can't contact us now.

389
00:20:59,321 --> 00:21:02,616
From here on, it depends on those two.

390
00:21:04,368 --> 00:21:06,995
-Um…
-What is it?

391
00:21:08,955 --> 00:21:13,335
Um, Luca, you came to Japan
to study abroad, right?

392
00:21:14,378 --> 00:21:16,296
-Yes.
-That's right.

393
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:18,215
Obtaining a medical license
in Japan is Luca's dream.

394
00:21:19,007 --> 00:21:21,635
But for a student about to study
abroad long-term,

395
00:21:21,718 --> 00:21:23,970
I don't see any study material here.

396
00:21:24,846 --> 00:21:25,931
What?

397
00:21:26,556 --> 00:21:29,309
Not a single medical textbook
or reference book.

398
00:21:32,396 --> 00:21:34,689
I was planning to get them in Japan.

399
00:21:36,191 --> 00:21:37,651
Is that so?

400
00:21:43,281 --> 00:21:46,159
Regarding your study abroad,
I have a question as well.

401
00:21:46,243 --> 00:21:49,371
Luca, have you already paid
the tuition for your school?

402
00:21:51,206 --> 00:21:53,417
Of course he has. Right?

403
00:21:53,917 --> 00:21:58,630
The documents earlier contained neither
a payment confirmation nor a receipt.

404
00:21:59,256 --> 00:22:01,591
Even an email would be enough.
Do you have anything?

405
00:22:04,219 --> 00:22:05,220
Luca?

406
00:22:06,805 --> 00:22:09,224
If we cannot confirm
the reality of your studies,

407
00:22:09,307 --> 00:22:11,476
we cannot permit entry into the country.

408
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,687
Huh? He can't enter Japan?

409
00:22:15,939 --> 00:22:17,441
That's great news.

410
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:19,484
You paid it, right?

411
00:22:20,026 --> 00:22:22,696
Luca, check your account.

412
00:22:23,321 --> 00:22:24,698
-Right now?
-Yes.

413
00:22:25,615 --> 00:22:27,033
-Here?
-Yes.

414
00:22:30,912 --> 00:22:33,331
-Hey.
-Just give it to me.

415
00:22:37,627 --> 00:22:39,379
Here, open it.

416
00:22:44,885 --> 00:22:45,802
21,136 YEN

417
00:22:45,886 --> 00:22:46,761
It's gone.

418
00:22:47,971 --> 00:22:49,472
Why isn't it here?

419
00:22:50,015 --> 00:22:52,100
I'm sure I transferred it here!
Twenty million yen!

420
00:22:54,519 --> 00:22:55,478
T-Twenty million?

421
00:22:55,562 --> 00:22:57,939
That's a massive amount.

422
00:22:58,023 --> 00:23:00,483
Tsuzuki, you gave that much to Luca?

423
00:23:02,944 --> 00:23:04,696
What's wrong with that?

424
00:23:05,488 --> 00:23:08,033
Luca had student loan debt back home

425
00:23:08,116 --> 00:23:10,243
and was about to give up
on becoming a doctor.

426
00:23:10,869 --> 00:23:16,291
That's why I decided to support
his tuition and living expenses.

427
00:23:16,374 --> 00:23:20,170
That's a typical textbook scam.

428
00:23:23,465 --> 00:23:26,426
I'm paying for everything.

429
00:23:27,093 --> 00:23:28,428
-What?
-What?

430
00:23:29,137 --> 00:23:32,474
His travel expenses,
living costs in Japan,

431
00:23:32,557 --> 00:23:34,684
all of it is paid by me. Right?

432
00:23:34,768 --> 00:23:36,895
It's just a temporary advance.

433
00:23:36,978 --> 00:23:39,856
I happened to tie up my funds
for a major purchase recently.

434
00:23:40,398 --> 00:23:42,734
I hope your work goes smoothly.

435
00:23:42,817 --> 00:23:44,903
Aoi, thank you.

436
00:23:46,404 --> 00:23:48,865
In this case, it's also the woman paying.

437
00:23:51,201 --> 00:23:55,664
These two men are looking
more and more similar.

438
00:23:55,747 --> 00:23:57,290
Hey, Luca.

439
00:23:57,374 --> 00:23:58,959
Where did my money go?

440
00:23:59,668 --> 00:24:01,962
Did you splurge it all away or something?

441
00:24:02,045 --> 00:24:03,546
Be honest.

442
00:24:09,761 --> 00:24:10,971
Give me that.

443
00:24:12,264 --> 00:24:14,057
Akane? Who's that?

444
00:24:17,227 --> 00:24:20,230
Is she your lover in Japan?

445
00:24:21,022 --> 00:24:23,358
Was she the real reason you came to Japan?

446
00:24:23,942 --> 00:24:26,111
How much longer
are you planning to trick Toko?

447
00:24:26,194 --> 00:24:28,571
-Gunji…
-Um…

448
00:24:29,322 --> 00:24:31,950
I have one request.

449
00:24:36,913 --> 00:24:39,165
I want to inspect
the ingredients of those pills.

450
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:41,501
The pills?

451
00:24:41,584 --> 00:24:44,004
Yes. The ones Tsuzuki was taking.

452
00:24:44,796 --> 00:24:48,883
I've been wondering the whole time
whether they're really just supplements.

453
00:24:56,266 --> 00:24:57,726
How are you going to inspect them?

454
00:25:01,771 --> 00:25:04,482
Entered the underground passage.
ETA about ten minutes.

455
00:25:04,566 --> 00:25:07,235
Roger that. We've got an entry plan.

456
00:25:11,573 --> 00:25:13,199
This is Matsuyama.

457
00:25:13,283 --> 00:25:16,119
I'm the only one standing
in front of the door.

458
00:25:20,206 --> 00:25:22,542
I am going to open the door now.

459
00:25:23,251 --> 00:25:25,253
Don't try anything funny.

460
00:25:26,004 --> 00:25:26,921
I won't.

461
00:25:32,052 --> 00:25:33,428
Slowly, okay?

462
00:25:34,471 --> 00:25:35,555
Okay.

463
00:25:50,111 --> 00:25:51,780
When am I getting my fountain pen back?

464
00:25:51,863 --> 00:25:54,532
-Leon, please calm down.
-The police are about to come in, right?

465
00:25:54,616 --> 00:25:56,451
-Wait!
-What if it gets scratched?

466
00:25:56,534 --> 00:25:57,869
Police?

467
00:26:01,414 --> 00:26:02,374
Mori.

468
00:26:06,378 --> 00:26:08,004
My goodness.

469
00:26:09,881 --> 00:26:11,132
This is bad.

470
00:26:11,216 --> 00:26:12,592
Why is the police coming?!

471
00:26:13,218 --> 00:26:15,762
So you were using this
to snitch to them after all!

472
00:26:15,845 --> 00:26:18,223
-No…
-Don't lie to me, you bastard!

473
00:26:18,306 --> 00:26:22,435
You were pretending to cooperate
just to buy time!

474
00:26:22,519 --> 00:26:24,562
-That's not true. I'm--
-Shut up!

475
00:26:24,646 --> 00:26:26,731
I can't trust any of you anymore!

476
00:26:26,815 --> 00:26:29,150
-Gunji!
-It isn't over yet!

477
00:26:30,735 --> 00:26:31,736
It isn't over?

478
00:26:33,279 --> 00:26:34,489
T-The inspection.

479
00:26:35,115 --> 00:26:37,867
There is still a place we haven't checked.

480
00:26:38,827 --> 00:26:40,036
Mori.

481
00:26:46,126 --> 00:26:46,960
Please look.

482
00:26:47,961 --> 00:26:50,296
-Look in this bag.
-What's that?

483
00:26:52,298 --> 00:26:53,466
May I open it?

484
00:26:53,550 --> 00:26:55,468
-Wait--
-Don't move!

485
00:26:57,137 --> 00:26:58,096
Open it.

486
00:27:02,642 --> 00:27:03,852
Pardon me.

487
00:27:15,905 --> 00:27:18,450
-"Dear Luca"?
-Give it back!

488
00:27:26,958 --> 00:27:28,334
"To my beloved Luca.

489
00:27:28,418 --> 00:27:31,129
If anything should happen to me,

490
00:27:31,212 --> 00:27:36,009
I bequeath my corporate shares
and all my assets to you,

491
00:27:36,092 --> 00:27:38,803
Luca Bennett."

492
00:27:41,973 --> 00:27:43,600
What is this?

493
00:27:45,477 --> 00:27:48,730
Is it a will?

494
00:27:49,272 --> 00:27:53,193
No, there's no date,
so it doesn't seem to be formal.

495
00:27:55,445 --> 00:27:57,197
I was just organizing my feelings

496
00:27:58,239 --> 00:28:00,492
before consulting a lawyer.

497
00:28:00,575 --> 00:28:02,160
Feelings?

498
00:28:03,495 --> 00:28:05,497
Forget about 20 million.

499
00:28:05,580 --> 00:28:08,208
You intended to give
this guy all your assets?

500
00:28:10,210 --> 00:28:12,462
You knew that?

501
00:28:12,545 --> 00:28:14,881
When I wrote this, that was my intention.

502
00:28:16,674 --> 00:28:18,176
I wanted to support Luca's dream

503
00:28:19,469 --> 00:28:21,221
and thought of it as proof of love.

504
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:25,642
But now I don't know anymore.

505
00:28:27,644 --> 00:28:29,521
You didn't pay the tuition.

506
00:28:30,063 --> 00:28:32,815
You won't say where
the 20 million went either.

507
00:28:33,525 --> 00:28:37,654
Nor the real reason you came to Japan.

508
00:28:39,322 --> 00:28:40,406
Hey.

509
00:28:41,074 --> 00:28:43,076
What is the meaning of this, Luca?

510
00:28:52,752 --> 00:28:54,838
The test results
for the medicine just came back.

511
00:28:55,505 --> 00:28:58,383
A component called
norglycemide was detected.

512
00:28:59,259 --> 00:29:01,135
Norglycemide.

513
00:29:01,970 --> 00:29:03,263
What's that?

514
00:29:03,346 --> 00:29:05,932
It's certainly not an ingredient
in a beauty supplement.

515
00:29:06,015 --> 00:29:07,976
It strongly affects the body's metabolism,

516
00:29:08,059 --> 00:29:10,770
and if overdosed, carries a risk
of inducing a coma.

517
00:29:10,854 --> 00:29:13,273
Worst case, it could be life-threatening.

518
00:29:13,982 --> 00:29:15,233
Life-threatening?

519
00:29:15,775 --> 00:29:19,779
You weren't just tricking Toko,
you were trying to kill her?

520
00:29:19,863 --> 00:29:21,781
No, I would never--

521
00:29:21,865 --> 00:29:23,449
If Toko dies, you get all her assets.

522
00:29:23,533 --> 00:29:26,119
Then, with that Akane woman in Japan…

523
00:29:29,831 --> 00:29:31,833
-Toko…
-Enough!

524
00:29:32,750 --> 00:29:34,919
I was such a fool.

525
00:29:36,212 --> 00:29:38,214
I blindly assumed it was fate.

526
00:29:39,966 --> 00:29:41,342
TO MY BELOVED LUCA

527
00:29:44,971 --> 00:29:46,472
I'm glad I found out…

528
00:29:48,016 --> 00:29:49,475
before it came to this.

529
00:29:55,940 --> 00:29:57,025
Um…

530
00:29:59,444 --> 00:30:01,654
Why did you write

531
00:30:03,031 --> 00:30:04,908
that will?

532
00:30:07,410 --> 00:30:11,289
You said it was "proof of love",

533
00:30:11,873 --> 00:30:15,835
but I don't understand love

534
00:30:15,919 --> 00:30:17,962
very well,

535
00:30:19,255 --> 00:30:20,632
so I wanted you to tell me.

536
00:30:27,096 --> 00:30:28,514
I told you

537
00:30:29,474 --> 00:30:33,770
I collapsed a year ago
in the Unitia Federation, right?

538
00:30:34,812 --> 00:30:39,192
Yes. Luca happened to pass by
and helped you.

539
00:30:40,777 --> 00:30:42,820
I found that out later.

540
00:30:43,488 --> 00:30:44,405
The truth is,

541
00:30:45,114 --> 00:30:47,367
my vision suddenly went dark,

542
00:30:47,909 --> 00:30:49,535
and I lost consciousness right then.

543
00:30:50,536 --> 00:30:51,371
What?

544
00:30:53,247 --> 00:30:55,083
I recovered at first,

545
00:30:56,125 --> 00:30:59,212
but after that,
I kept getting cold sweats,

546
00:30:59,712 --> 00:31:00,672
my hands shook.

547
00:31:02,382 --> 00:31:04,634
I got sick over and over.

548
00:31:05,301 --> 00:31:06,678
Back then,

549
00:31:08,012 --> 00:31:10,765
I seriously thought I might die.

550
00:31:12,183 --> 00:31:13,226
But…

551
00:31:16,688 --> 00:31:21,442
even after helping me,
Luca took care of me.

552
00:31:24,153 --> 00:31:26,114
I wanted to thank him,

553
00:31:26,197 --> 00:31:27,865
so I supported him in my own way.

554
00:31:28,825 --> 00:31:30,618
The will was the same.

555
00:31:32,870 --> 00:31:33,997
It felt like…

556
00:31:39,419 --> 00:31:41,254
Luca gave me my life back.

557
00:31:51,806 --> 00:31:54,600
Um, Tsuzuki.

558
00:31:57,353 --> 00:31:59,355
Regarding those symptoms,

559
00:31:59,439 --> 00:32:02,775
did you also experience
palpitations or intense hunger?

560
00:32:03,359 --> 00:32:04,444
I did.

561
00:32:04,944 --> 00:32:05,987
How did you know?

562
00:32:07,196 --> 00:32:08,990
Those are symptoms of hypoglycemia.

563
00:32:09,073 --> 00:32:12,076
The medicine earlier, norglycemide,

564
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:14,412
acts to raise blood sugar levels.

565
00:32:14,495 --> 00:32:17,707
While dangerous for healthy individuals,
if your blood sugar drops too low,

566
00:32:17,790 --> 00:32:19,834
it serves as medicine to prevent attacks.

567
00:32:20,460 --> 00:32:24,297
Then this guy was trying to…

568
00:32:24,380 --> 00:32:27,258
Rather than trying to kill you,

569
00:32:28,593 --> 00:32:31,095
maybe he was trying to protect you.

570
00:32:34,515 --> 00:32:36,851
Why did you stay silent about that?

571
00:32:38,811 --> 00:32:42,815
Was there a circumstance
that kept you from speaking?

572
00:32:48,279 --> 00:32:49,530
Tell me.

573
00:32:57,705 --> 00:32:58,873
Toko.

574
00:33:05,254 --> 00:33:06,589
You have a tumor

575
00:33:07,507 --> 00:33:09,050
in your pancreas.

576
00:33:09,967 --> 00:33:11,219
A tumor?

577
00:33:11,844 --> 00:33:14,013
It has already spread to your liver.

578
00:33:14,764 --> 00:33:17,558
It's too advanced to remove surgically.

579
00:33:20,937 --> 00:33:24,023
Is it incurable?

580
00:33:24,732 --> 00:33:28,319
I've tried to tell you many times,
but you said you didn't want to hear it

581
00:33:28,402 --> 00:33:30,029
until things settled down at work.

582
00:33:38,454 --> 00:33:39,997
Toko!

583
00:33:41,499 --> 00:33:43,459
-Toko!
-Are you all right?

584
00:33:47,922 --> 00:33:49,215
Luca.

585
00:33:49,966 --> 00:33:51,342
Toko, can you hear me?

586
00:33:51,425 --> 00:33:52,593
What are those candies?

587
00:33:52,677 --> 00:33:54,345
It's glucose.

588
00:33:55,972 --> 00:33:57,515
Chew them slowly.

589
00:33:58,266 --> 00:34:00,601
Now, let's slow the breathing down.

590
00:34:07,441 --> 00:34:10,570
Breathe out slowly. That's it.

591
00:34:12,155 --> 00:34:13,239
You're okay.

592
00:34:14,574 --> 00:34:16,033
She's calming down.

593
00:34:17,702 --> 00:34:19,871
Let me call the hospital, just to be safe.

594
00:34:20,621 --> 00:34:21,789
The hospital?

595
00:34:25,626 --> 00:34:28,296
Does this "Akane"

596
00:34:29,338 --> 00:34:30,423
refer to the hospital?

597
00:34:31,215 --> 00:34:32,258
Huh?

598
00:34:38,389 --> 00:34:39,891
This is Akane Medical Center.

599
00:34:40,433 --> 00:34:42,101
This is Luca Bennett.

600
00:34:42,185 --> 00:34:44,353
I'm calling again about Toko Tsuzuki.

601
00:34:45,313 --> 00:34:47,565
Please put me through
to her doctor, Shidagama.

602
00:34:47,648 --> 00:34:49,233
So that's what it was.

603
00:34:51,819 --> 00:34:55,239
Then everything was for Toko's sake?

604
00:34:55,323 --> 00:34:57,575
-Her blood pressure has dropped again.
-It appears so.

605
00:34:57,658 --> 00:34:59,535
‎Currently applying first-aid
‎as quickly as I can.

606
00:35:00,328 --> 00:35:03,873
Luca isn't a scammer at all.

607
00:35:03,956 --> 00:35:05,750
He was caring for Toko the whole time.

608
00:35:05,833 --> 00:35:06,751
Iuchi!

609
00:35:07,460 --> 00:35:09,545
The tactical unit has arrived.

610
00:35:15,927 --> 00:35:16,886
What's the situation?

611
00:35:16,969 --> 00:35:19,305
Inside the secondary room,
one suspect, four hostages.

612
00:35:19,388 --> 00:35:20,932
-Get into position.
-Yes, sir.

613
00:35:22,516 --> 00:35:24,435
Could you hold off for a bit?

614
00:35:25,269 --> 00:35:27,438
I am Iuchi
from the International Crime Division.

615
00:35:28,814 --> 00:35:30,274
The situation inside has changed.

616
00:35:30,858 --> 00:35:32,693
The suspect is starting to calm down.

617
00:35:32,777 --> 00:35:35,696
Right now, Gate 24 staff

618
00:35:35,780 --> 00:35:37,657
are risking their lives
to resolve things inside.

619
00:35:38,282 --> 00:35:40,076
I understand. Thank you very much.

620
00:35:43,287 --> 00:35:44,288
Luca.

621
00:35:47,083 --> 00:35:48,960
What about the money I gave you?

622
00:35:54,757 --> 00:35:55,925
It seems

623
00:35:57,051 --> 00:36:00,888
all of it went toward
your medical expenses, Tsuzuki.

624
00:36:04,058 --> 00:36:06,394
Medication, consultation requests

625
00:36:06,477 --> 00:36:10,481
to the medical center,
preparations for tests and treatment.

626
00:36:11,107 --> 00:36:12,650
Including future expenses,

627
00:36:13,401 --> 00:36:16,988
he likely didn't spend
a single yen on himself.

628
00:36:18,906 --> 00:36:20,908
One more thing.

629
00:36:21,993 --> 00:36:23,077
Luca.

630
00:36:24,078 --> 00:36:28,082
You got a job at Akane Medical Center,
didn't you?

631
00:36:28,165 --> 00:36:29,041
What?

632
00:36:33,087 --> 00:36:36,799
Helping foreign patients
and assisting with medical examinations.

633
00:36:37,967 --> 00:36:39,010
Of course,

634
00:36:39,093 --> 00:36:42,888
you will need to pass through Immigration
again, with the proper procedures.

635
00:36:47,059 --> 00:36:48,185
Then,

636
00:36:49,687 --> 00:36:52,398
for your living expenses in Japan,

637
00:36:52,481 --> 00:36:55,109
you intend to earn them yourself?

638
00:36:57,153 --> 00:36:58,654
Why?

639
00:36:58,738 --> 00:37:00,197
Like I said before,

640
00:37:01,699 --> 00:37:04,076
you've always been there for me.

641
00:37:04,702 --> 00:37:06,704
Now I want to be there for you.

642
00:37:11,417 --> 00:37:13,085
I don't want your inheritance.

643
00:37:14,420 --> 00:37:16,589
You don't have to stay with me.

644
00:37:19,342 --> 00:37:20,509
Please…

645
00:37:23,971 --> 00:37:25,806
put your health first.

646
00:37:49,914 --> 00:37:50,748
Toko.

647
00:37:53,084 --> 00:37:55,252
I didn't notice a single thing.

648
00:37:59,340 --> 00:38:00,716
I'm sorry.

649
00:38:22,571 --> 00:38:23,948
This is Hayami.

650
00:38:25,783 --> 00:38:29,036
Gunji has surrendered his weapon.
He has no intent to resist.

651
00:38:30,621 --> 00:38:31,664
I am opening the door.

652
00:38:40,631 --> 00:38:41,841
On your knees!

653
00:38:41,924 --> 00:38:42,925
-Search him.
-Roger.

654
00:38:43,008 --> 00:38:44,427
On the floor!

655
00:38:45,594 --> 00:38:46,929
Nothing on him.

656
00:39:06,031 --> 00:39:10,327
Apparently, the person who reported
a scammer on this flight was Gunji.

657
00:39:10,411 --> 00:39:11,787
Gunji?

658
00:39:11,871 --> 00:39:14,290
Thanks to that,
we were able to get this far.

659
00:39:15,124 --> 00:39:16,834
Well, in reality,

660
00:39:16,917 --> 00:39:19,253
-the actual scammer was someone else.
-Look!

661
00:39:19,336 --> 00:39:20,212
This scratch!

662
00:39:20,296 --> 00:39:22,339
What have you done?

663
00:39:22,423 --> 00:39:25,593
We need to confiscate it as a weapon.

664
00:39:25,676 --> 00:39:28,345
Do you realize how valuable this item is?

665
00:39:31,307 --> 00:39:34,185
That fountain pen is not worth that much.

666
00:39:34,268 --> 00:39:35,561
Excuse me.

667
00:39:38,063 --> 00:39:41,150
Underneath the scratch,
another metal is visible.

668
00:39:41,233 --> 00:39:44,778
This is not solid gold.
It's plated on the surface.

669
00:39:45,404 --> 00:39:47,823
The decorative stone is also just glass.

670
00:39:49,533 --> 00:39:52,578
Also, we heard from Luca.

671
00:39:52,661 --> 00:39:54,413
Before coming here,

672
00:39:54,497 --> 00:39:57,541
you sold him a ring, right?

673
00:39:58,209 --> 00:40:00,586
You claimed it was a real sapphire.

674
00:40:00,669 --> 00:40:02,880
We have a lot of questions to ask you.

675
00:40:03,589 --> 00:40:04,840
Onodera.

676
00:40:07,801 --> 00:40:09,845
Most likely, that ring as well.

677
00:40:10,554 --> 00:40:12,348
I know.

678
00:40:13,015 --> 00:40:14,892
I can tell it's a fake.

679
00:40:15,893 --> 00:40:17,102
You knew?

680
00:40:17,186 --> 00:40:20,147
I called myself a CEO,

681
00:40:20,231 --> 00:40:22,399
but my company is small.
I'm the only employee.

682
00:40:23,275 --> 00:40:24,109
What?

683
00:40:24,610 --> 00:40:28,280
I want to hire people,
but things haven't gone well.

684
00:40:28,364 --> 00:40:31,825
So, perhaps you dated Leon…

685
00:40:32,576 --> 00:40:36,205
Not to find a marriage partner,
but an employee?

686
00:40:37,414 --> 00:40:38,666
Aoi?

687
00:40:44,547 --> 00:40:47,800
I knew you were full of lies.

688
00:40:49,593 --> 00:40:52,263
But your smooth talking and nerve,

689
00:40:52,346 --> 00:40:54,348
those at least were real.

690
00:40:55,474 --> 00:40:57,601
Tell everything to the police

691
00:40:58,561 --> 00:41:01,814
and make amends for what you've done.

692
00:41:02,940 --> 00:41:03,941
And then,

693
00:41:05,901 --> 00:41:08,487
if you intend to turn your life around…

694
00:41:10,447 --> 00:41:11,824
come to me.

695
00:41:16,579 --> 00:41:17,871
What's your answer?

696
00:41:21,208 --> 00:41:22,209
Yes.

697
00:41:27,339 --> 00:41:29,925
-Well then, right this way.
-Okay.

698
00:41:30,634 --> 00:41:33,345
May we talk to you as well, Onodera?

699
00:41:33,429 --> 00:41:34,305
Yes.

700
00:41:40,519 --> 00:41:41,562
Tsuzuki.

701
00:41:42,771 --> 00:41:44,857
Thank you for your help.

702
00:41:48,360 --> 00:41:51,488
I will pay Luca's tuition immediately.

703
00:41:51,572 --> 00:41:56,410
That will satisfy
the purpose of entry, right?

704
00:41:56,493 --> 00:41:57,328
Toko.

705
00:41:58,329 --> 00:41:59,163
‎Yes.

706
00:42:00,539 --> 00:42:01,707
Thank you very much.

707
00:42:08,881 --> 00:42:10,341
APPROVED BY IMMIGRATION

708
00:42:10,424 --> 00:42:11,634
Good luck.

709
00:42:11,717 --> 00:42:12,760
‎Thank you.

710
00:42:13,761 --> 00:42:15,763
-Here you are.
-Thank you very much.

711
00:42:18,140 --> 00:42:20,517
Welcome to Japan.

712
00:42:23,646 --> 00:42:25,022
‎Thank you.

713
00:42:36,700 --> 00:42:37,951
So this is love.

714
00:42:49,088 --> 00:42:52,091
-I'm glad they resolved it safely.
-Yes.

715
00:42:52,174 --> 00:42:53,884
Thanks to the brave people on the ground.

716
00:42:55,177 --> 00:42:57,971
You really seem to trust Gate 24.

717
00:42:58,597 --> 00:43:01,100
Yes. It's the team I built, after all.

718
00:43:01,975 --> 00:43:03,727
Your team, huh?

719
00:43:05,771 --> 00:43:09,650
I hope that trust is never betrayed.

720
00:43:10,317 --> 00:43:11,193
Goodbye.

721
00:43:44,727 --> 00:43:46,395
It's been a while, huh?

722
00:43:47,604 --> 00:43:48,814
What's going on?

723
00:43:49,606 --> 00:43:50,899
I have a favor to ask.

724
00:43:51,525 --> 00:43:54,278
I want you to look for a spy.

725
00:43:55,612 --> 00:43:56,530
What do you mean?

726
00:43:56,613 --> 00:43:59,450
We received a report
that for the past two months,

727
00:43:59,533 --> 00:44:02,828
there have been people involved
with terrorists and extremists

728
00:44:02,911 --> 00:44:04,455
entering the country at a rapid scale.

729
00:44:04,538 --> 00:44:08,125
Gate 24 has become
a shortcut for terrorists.

730
00:44:08,917 --> 00:44:11,253
There's a spy in Gate 24?

731
00:44:13,130 --> 00:44:14,339
I want you to look for that spy.

732
00:44:15,132 --> 00:44:16,467
I'm counting on you.

733
00:44:34,026 --> 00:44:35,235
Mori.

734
00:44:37,738 --> 00:44:38,989
Oh my.

735
00:44:44,119 --> 00:44:44,953
‎AT LAST, THE FINAL CHAPTER!

736
00:44:45,037 --> 00:44:47,080
‎Inspection is temporarily halted
‎at the moment.

737
00:44:47,164 --> 00:44:48,665
‎-I'm a doctor.
‎-Was it an accident,

738
00:44:48,749 --> 00:44:50,626
‎-or on purpose?
‎-‎Someone among us

739
00:44:50,709 --> 00:44:53,170
‎is in direct contact with a person
‎suspected of being a spy.

740
00:44:53,253 --> 00:44:56,673
‎If there really is a spy at Gate 24…

741
00:44:56,757 --> 00:44:59,009
‎-This is…
‎-Oh my.

742
00:44:59,092 --> 00:44:59,968
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

